The Contact Center Data Science team developed the Call Intent Classification Model, an advanced LLM-powered solution designed to automatically analyze and categorize customer touchpoints across multiple Lines of Business (LOBs), including Core Premier, Individual & Family Plans (IFP), and others.
Legacy manual or rigid keyword-based tracking methods struggled to capture nuanced customer needs, creating a blind spot in operational strategy. To solve this, the team leveraged Large Language Models (LLMs) to process and understand complex, multi-tier call intents from over 20,000+ conversation transcripts per LOB. By extracting semantic meaning, the model accurately classifies calls into granular, multi-tiered intent categories, providing deep visibility into why customers contact support.
A critical component of the project involved re-engineering the primary data ingestion pipeline. The legacy pipeline was slow, prone to failures, and unable to scale with the high volume of daily transcripts. By fixing the core architecture and optimizing the data flow, the team achieved an 80% reduction in operational infrastructure costs while drastically improving pipeline reliability and processing speed. 
